  "scope": "Replace private positive-divisibility wrapper with existing le_of_dvd",
  "validation": "Paired target and both tracked direct module clients pass, with current-source CommonUnit and StrongDivisibility provider pairs mapped to earlier receipts. Both client object pairs match. Three-object-pinned probes show five identical surviving target declaration/type/axiom blocks, one private removal and matching global simp/instances.",
  "limitations": [
    "The private le_of_positive_multiple declaration disappears. The qualified-name search covers tracked Lean/Python only, not external or dynamic references.",
    "Downstream HalfIndex, FirstIndex, AuxiliarySeed, OuterSeed and construction clients were not rebuilt in this lane; equal direct IndexDivisibility objects do not establish a full downstream replay.",
    "Project and package transitive dependencies remain cached. Matching direct producer pairs do not establish a fully current-source closure; census reports do not prove equality of every persistent environment extension or proof body.",
    "Single shared-load timing samples are not a general performance benchmark. Author source/build records are historical; included independent review/audit verify the commit and parent.",
    "Compiled objects and cached overlays are omitted; receipt hashes and paths require external objects for independent byte verification."
  ],
